   245	
   246	Reaching zero was iterative in a way worth reporting, since the
   247	iteration is the method. The comparison harness itself went through
   248	six adversarial review rounds before we trusted it: early versions
   249	could report vacuous agreement (a slim CI artifact corrupted totals; a
   250	column of zeros compared equal to a column of zeros it should never
   251	have matched), and the reviews killed those with mutation tests —
   252	deliberately corrupted inputs that a sound harness must catch. The
   253	final harness binds each panel row to a content digest, rebuilds
   254	byte-identically, and carries 2,396 tests. The number we report is
   255	only as good as the machinery that computed it, and the machinery's
   256	failure modes were hunted by a reviewer whose job was to break it.
   257	
   258	Two boundaries on the claim. First, conformance is agreement with a
   259	reference, and the reference is not ground truth — Section 4 shows it
   260	disagreeing with the instruments it tracks, which is precisely why the
   261	comparison stores derivations rather than trust. Second, the
   262	adversarial review that gated every merge in this work is independent
   263	in the cross-model sense (a different model family, prompted to
   264	refute, with its findings closed by machinery), but it is not external
   265	certification: reviewer and author sit inside the same project. A
   266	separately governed verification protocol is future work, and until it
   267	exists we state our verification as what it is.
   268	
   269	# 4. When the oracle disagrees: dispositions with legal derivations
   270	
   271	A conformance run that ends in disagreement forces a choice with three
   272	honest outcomes: the encoding is wrong (fix it), the reference is
   273	wrong (demonstrate it), or the two are answering different questions
   274	(declare it). The disposition machinery exists to make the second and
   275	third outcomes as auditable as the first. A disagreement attributed to
   276	the reference cannot be waved through; it requires either the
   277	reference maintainer's acceptance or an independent derivation from
   278	the governing instruments, recorded beside the cells it explains. The
   279	rule's purpose is to block the tempting failure mode — "our number
   280	differs, theirs is probably wrong" — by pricing that claim at a legal
   281	argument.
   282	
   283	Two derivations from this comparison illustrate the standard, and both
   284	became upstream reports.
   285	
   286	**A safeguard rate outliving its schedule.** The Section 201 solar
   287	safeguard's extension proclamation (10339) sets a staged duty
   288	schedule in its annex, verbatim: 14.75 percent through February 6,
   289	2023, then 14.5, then 14.25, then 14 percent through February 6,
   290	2026 — and nothing after. The current tariff schedule corroborates
   291	the end: the compiler's note on the affected headings reads "this
   292	subheading and its related note … have expired." The reference
   293	carries a flat 14.5 percent on the affected lines past the terminal
   294	date, which is wrong on two axes at once — 14.5 was the *second*
   295	year's rate, stale since February 2024, and every rate is expired
   296	after February 2026. Our encoding carries the staged schedule and
   297	its end, citing the proclamation's table; the disagreement covers
   298	every affected cell after the schedule moves. The derivation —
   299	proclamation, annex table, terminal date, the schedule's own expiry
   300	note — is recorded in the disposition file, and the finding was
   301	filed upstream with the same citations.
   302	
   303	**Four countries on the wrong rate column.** The tariff schedule's
   304	General Note 3(b) directs that "the rates of duty shown in column 2
   305	shall apply to products, whether imported directly or indirectly, of
   306	the following countries and areas": the Republic of Belarus, Cuba,
   307	North Korea, and the Russian Federation. The reference's parser has
   308	no column-2 branch, so those four countries inherit column-1 base
   309	rates throughout its panel. The disagreement is systematic rather
   310	than episodic — it touches every line for four partners — and the
   311	derivation is a single sentence of the schedule's own general notes,
   312	with the note's cross-reference to the Russia and Belarus additional-
   313	duty headings compounding the gap. Filed upstream likewise.
   314	
   315	We report both findings as what they are: derivation-backed and, as of
   316	this writing, unacknowledged. The reports sit in the tracker's issue
   317	queue with four others we filed en route — a locale-sensitivity bug
   318	that corrupted country matching (with a patch), the measured build
   319	envelope of Section 3, and a proposal that the project publish its
   320	panel as a release artifact, which would let every downstream user
   321	skip the 123 GiB build we measured. None of this is offered as fault-
   322	finding. A reference strong enough to validate against is a reference
   323	worth strengthening, and the economics of the exchange favor everyone:
   324	the tracker gave us the spine that made our zero meaningful, and the
   325	conformance run gave the tracker two defects located to the instrument
   326	and the line, for free.
   327	
   328	The dispositions are the paper's answer to a question every validation
   329	exercise should face: what happens to your zero when the reference is
   330	imperfect? An unexplained-zero predicate against an imperfect
   331	reference is achievable only with an escape valve, and the escape
   332	valve is where validation exercises usually rot. Ours is load-bearing
   333	and inspectable — every escaped cell names its instrument — and the
   334	tripwires of Section 3 patrol its edges. When the reference updates,
   335	the dispositions are re-litigated against the new panel, not
   336	grandfathered: acceptance upstream would convert them to fixed cells;
   337	a counter-derivation would convert them to encoding bugs. Either
   338	outcome improves the public record, which is the point of validating
   339	in the open.
   340	
   341	# 5. Synthetic customs entries from official margins
   342	
   343	The statutory panel answers what the rate was. Applying it to trade
   344	requires the other half: what crossed the border, at what value, in
   345	which tariff line, from where. The public record answers this at the
   346	margin — monthly totals by line, country, and district — while the
   347	transaction-level record (the entry summaries importers actually file)
   348	is either restricted to secure-enclave access or not assembled at all.
   349	We release the bridge: a synthetic transaction-level dataset that
   350	reproduces the public margins exactly and declares every assumption it
   351	adds on the way down to entry grain.
   352	
   353	**The margins, from the loading dock rather than the front door.**
   354	Census publishes the complete monthly U.S. Imports of Merchandise
   355	database as public archives — one ZIP per month, no authentication, at
   356	a stable URL pattern. Eighteen archives (January 2025 through June
   357	2026, ~3.3 GB, every byte sha-manifested at retrieval) parse under the
   358	record layouts shipped inside the archives themselves into 38,841,305
   359	detail rows: tariff line × partner country × customs district × month,
   360	with twenty-two monthly measures spanning customs value, dutiable
   361	value, calculated duty, charges, quantities, and air/vessel/
   362	containerized transport splits. The same archives carry the
   363	publisher's own control-total files, which makes reconciliation an
   364	internal affair: our parse must reproduce Census's own totals, in
   365	integer dollars, on three independent axes — by country, by commodity,
   366	by district. Across all eighteen months and every published measure,
   367	it does, with zero tolerance and zero failures. The archives replace
   368	an API path we built first and demoted: the equivalent extraction
   369	through the Census International Trade API took thousands of calls and
   370	failed server-side on the largest chapters, and the bulk files carry
   371	strictly more detail. The API survives as something better than a
   372	primary source — an independent second channel. A gated cross-check
   373	fetches a stratified sample through the API and compares cell for
   374	cell: 108,977 cells, exact on all four dollar measures, zero
   375	mismatches. Two official channels agreeing is stronger provenance
   376	than either alone.
   377	
   378	**Down to entries, assumptions on the table.** The generator
   379	disaggregates each (line × country × month) customs-value cell into
   380	weighted synthetic entries. The identity constraint is absolute:
   381	weighted customs value reproduces every cell to the integer dollar, on
   382	an enforced domain (cell values at or below 2^53, where integer
   383	arithmetic is exact; the build asserts the reproduction at run time
   384	rather than trusting the construction). In the pilot window of
   385	February through June 2026 — chosen to sit inside the composed
   386	statutory spine's domain — 3,806,050 entry rows carry 44,881,145
   387	weighted entries and a weighted customs value of $1,467,109,590,515,
   388	equal to the window's margins total exactly.
   389	
   390	What the margins do not determine, the dataset does not pretend to
   391	know. An assumptions register ships beside the data, and its entries
   392	are calibrated where an anchor exists and labeled where one does not:
   393	entry counts derive from Customs and Border Protection's published
   394	fiscal-year-to-date mean entry value, with the coverage window
   395	(October 1, 2025 through July 27, 2026) carried explicitly rather than
   396	laundered into an annual figure; within-cell entry sizes are
   397	lognormal, with σ = 2.6916 solved so that the share of entries at or
   398	under $2,500 matches CBP's published informal-entry share — labeled a
   399	proxy moment, because the regulatory informal-entry categories map
   400	imperfectly onto a value threshold, and the residual gap is registered
   401	(achieved share within 2.6 × 10⁻⁵ of target; achieved mean $32,689
   402	against a $32,916 anchor, the difference a documented small-cell floor
   403	effect). Three fields have no public anchor at all — postal-shipment
   404	status, sub-monthly timing, the shipment-value/customs-value
   405	distinction — and each is set to a declared constant with a
   406	sensitivity note, not imputed and forgotten. Every row carries
   407	`is_synthetic = true`.
   408	
   409	The honesty machinery extends to the anchors themselves. CBP's
   410	statistics page mixes completed fiscal years with in-progress ones;
   411	our parser emits in-progress years only as fiscal-year-to-date records
   412	with explicit as-of endpoints, and it fails closed — wording it cannot
   413	read, impossible calendar dates, notes displaced from their table,
   414	endpoints later than the retrieval instant, all raise rather than
   415	default. A fiscal year becomes an annual total only after its final
   416	day has elapsed.
   417	
   418	The result is not a substitute for the restricted transaction data,
   419	and the paper does not offer it as one. It is the dataset that
   420	downstream tariff microsimulation actually needs: entry-grain records
   421	whose margins are exactly the official ones, whose every departure
   422	from the observable record is enumerated, and whose fields conform to
   423	the statutory spine's input contract — so that the panel of Section 3
   424	and these entries compose into duty computation at the grain where
   425	duties are assessed.
   426	
   427	# 6. Provenance engineering
   428	
   429	Every number in this paper is recomputable from public artifacts, and
   430	the machinery that makes that true was built by AI agents. We state
   431	both facts plainly because together they are the methods section: the
   432	pipeline's outputs are only trustworthy because its architecture
   433	assumes its authors — human or model — will err, and gates
   434	accordingly.
   435	
   436	**The gates.** Corpus documents enter under signed manifests; an
   437	encoding cannot cite what the corpus does not hold. Every rule change
   438	must compile, must carry proof atoms whose excerpts appear in the
   439	cited document, and must pass companion tests that pin behavior at its
   440	effective boundaries — the merge machinery refuses the change
   441	otherwise. Panel derivations bind each row to a content digest and
   442	rebuild byte-identically. Conformance reports pin the reference
   443	commit, the engine build, and the encoding revision they were computed
   444	from, and the scoreboard numbers quoted in this paper carry their
   445	snapshot hashes because the live reports refresh as the encoding
   446	grows.
   447	
   448	**The adversary.** Every substantive change merged in this work
   449	passed independent adversarial review by a different model family,
   450	prompted to refute rather than confirm, with each finding closed by a
   451	code change and a test that fails on the pre-fix implementation —
   452	mutation-proven, not narrated. The entries pipeline of Section 5 is
   453	the instructive case: its publication machinery (atomic directory
   454	replacement with crash recovery) went through eight consecutive review
   455	rounds, each finding a strictly narrower defect class than the last —
   456	symlink-target validation before recursive deletion, a race in lock
   457	takeover, asynchronous exceptions landing after a rename's commit
   458	point, rename durability ordering under power loss — until the final
   459	round found the structural invariant the piecewise fixes had been
   460	approximating: no recovery marker may be removed until every mutation
   461	it records is durable. The reviewer's last pass swept every marker-
   462	removal site against that invariant, verified the closing test fails
   463	on the previous implementation, and returned no findings. We report
   464	the trajectory rather than just the endpoint because the trajectory is
   465	the evidence: a review process that converges to zero by narrowing
   466	finding classes is doing something different from one that runs out of
   467	patience.
   468	
   469	**The division of labor.** Model-written code, model-run reviews,
   470	machine-checked gates — and human judgment exactly where it is load-
   471	bearing: scope decisions (what counts as law versus estimation), the
   472	disposition standard of Section 4, anything that leaves the project
   473	(upstream reports, this paper), and the decision to ship. We do not
   474	claim the review regime is external certification; Section 3 states
   475	that boundary. We do claim the artifact trail is complete enough that
   476	a skeptic need not trust any of it: the encodings, the corpus
   477	manifests, the comparison harness, the entries pipeline, the review
   478	verdicts, and the evidence packs (build reports, reconciliation
   479	records, cross-check reports) are public, pinned, and re-runnable.
   480	
   481	The synthesis bears stating once, directly. The reason 2025–26 tariff
   482	law could be encoded, validated to unexplained-zero, and released with
   483	transaction-grain data inside the same year the law was moving is that
   484	the marginal cost of rigor collapsed: agents wrote the 149-test
   485	battery nobody budgets human-weeks for, re-derived the panel on every
   486	change, and re-litigated every disagreement against primary
   487	instruments. The gates are what let that speed compound instead of
   488	compounding error.
   489	
   490	# 7. Uses and limits
   491	
   492	What the pair enables now. The statutory panel and the synthetic
   493	entries share a contract — the entries' fields conform to the
   494	composed spine's inputs — so duty computation runs at entry grain:
   495	for any entry, the rate stack in force on its date, by authority,
   496	with the derivation attached. That supports revenue accounting by
   497	statutory component under any counterfactual expressible as dated
   498	rules (repeal an authority, move a termination date, extend a staged
   499	schedule), audit-grade rate lookup for any line × country × date in
   500	the covered window, and calibration: the ingest's 302,318 consumer

