   504	
   505	What the pair does not claim. No effective rates: trade-share
   506	weighting, exemption utilization, and de minimis composition are
   507	estimation, deliberately out of the conformance scope of Section 3.
   508	No incidence and no behavioral response: nothing here says who bears
   509	a duty or how trade reallocates when one changes; the entries
   510	reproduce observed margins under declared assumptions and do not
   511	model responses to counterfactuals. Computed duty at statutory rates
   512	is not collected revenue: exclusions in litigation, drawback,
   513	misclassification, and the wind-down mechanics of terminated
   514	authorities all wedge between the two, and our own comparison treats
   515	calculated-duty fields as related-never-gating for exactly this
   516	reason. The synthetic entries are not the restricted transaction
   517	record: within-cell structure below the margins is assumption, the
   518	register says which assumption, and analyses that depend on within-
   519	cell joint distributions (entry-size inequality, importer
   520	concentration) should not run on them. The covered window is January
   521	2025 through June 2026 for margins and the composed spine's domain
   522	(February 2026 onward) for entry-level duty computation; the panel's
   523	temporal debt outside the encoded domain is surfaced, not covered.
   524	
   525	The natural next analyses — distributional incidence of the 2025–26
   526	stack, tariff-revenue swaps against other instruments — sit one layer
   527	up, where these statutory computations meet household and firm
   528	microdata. That layer exists in our stack but is not this paper, and
   529	conflating the two would launder modeling assumptions through a
   530	dataset whose claim to exactness is precisely that it added none it
   531	did not declare.
   532	
   533	# 8. Related work
   534	
   535	**Tariff-rate data for the trade-war literature.** The empirical
   536	literature on the 2018–19 tariffs built its rate data by hand, wave by
   537	wave. Fajgelbaum, Goldberg, Kennedy, and Khandelwal digitized each
   538	wave's product lists and statutory rates from the official
   539	announcements to estimate the trade war's incidence
   540	[fajgelbaum2020return]; Amiti, Redding, and Weinstein assembled the
   541	same sequence for pass-through event studies [amiti2019impact;
   542	amiti2020whos]; Flaaen and Pierce mapped tariff-line changes into
   543	industry exposure measures [flaaen2019disentangling]. In each case the
   544	tariff schedule is a bespoke research input, frozen at publication.
   545	Bown's widely used trackers institutionalized the hand-compiled
   546	approach as a maintained public timeline [bown2021uschina;
   547	bown_piie_chart]. The 2025–26 environment strains this tradition on
   548	two margins the earlier waves mostly spared it: authority count
   549	(seven overlapping legal bases with distinct lifecycles) and tempo
   550	(terminations, expiries, and revision-level rate surgery inside single
   551	months). Teti's Global Tariff Database extends statutory rate coverage
   552	impressively in space and time — two hundred importers back to 1988 —
   553	but at HS-6, without the 2025–26 emergency authorities, and as data
   554	rather than executable derivations [teti2024missing].
   555	
   556	**The tracker we validate against.** The nearest neighbor to our
   557	statutory panel is its own validation reference. Yale Budget Lab's
   558	tariff-rate-tracker is an open-source pipeline producing an
   559	interval-encoded panel of statutory rates at the tariff-line ×
   560	country level for the 2025–26 regime, built from the trade
   561	commission's schedule archives with documented policy parameters
   562	[yaletracker_repo; budgetlab2026tracker]; the Budget Lab's rate
   563	series are already the benchmark other measurement work checks
   564	against [cavallo2026tracking]. We are not, therefore, the first
   565	executable statutory tariff panel; the tracker is one, and a good
   566	one. The contribution is the form and what the form enables: rules
   567	at the instrument grain, each version citing and quoting its legal
   568	source, with mandatory boundary tests — versus one pipeline whose
   569	judgment calls live in code — and, on top of that form, a
   570	cross-implementation conformance regime. To our knowledge the
   571	conformance run of Section 3 is the first external research
   572	engagement with the tracker's internals (we find no formal citation
   573	of the tool itself as of August 2026), and Section 4's
   574	derivation-backed defect reports are what that engagement produces
   575	when a disagreement survives audit.
   576	
   577	**Rules as code and calculator validation.** Executable encodings of
   578	law have an established line: OpenFisca's deployed tax-benefit
   579	engines [openfisca], Catala's formally grounded statute-to-code
   580	language [merigoux2021catala], and the policy agenda articulated for
   581	rules-as-code generally [mohun2020cracking]. Cross-validation is
   582	likewise institutionalized practice in tax microsimulation — NBER's
   583	TAXSIM as a reference implementation [feenberg1993introduction],
   584	EUROMOD's country-report validation regime [sutherland2013euromod],
   585	and maintained harnesses that reconcile independent calculators
   586	line-by-line [taxcalculator_taxsim_validation]. That culture has not
   587	previously reached trade law. Tariffs are, if anything, the easier
   588	target for it — the instruments are public, the schedule is versioned
   589	by the issuing agency, and the reference tracker already exists — and
   590	the 2025–26 record supplies the volatility that makes the exercise
   591	informative rather than ornamental.
   592	
   593	**Synthetic microdata.** The synthetic-data tradition in official
   594	statistics runs through disclosure avoidance: synthetic establishment
   595	panels standing in for confidential business registers
   596	[kinney2011towards], noise-infused releases with formal privacy
   597	guarantees [machanavajjhala2008privacy], and, in transport and
   598	demography, synthetic populations fit to published margins
   599	[beckman1996creating]. Customs data specifically have seen synthesis
   600	for machine-learning research — artificial Korean import declarations
   601	generated for fraud-detection benchmarks [jeong2022customs] — while
   602	the true U.S. transaction record remains restricted-access
   603	[bernard2009importers; census_lfttd] or proprietary. Our entries
   604	invert the disclosure-avoidance objective: the inputs are already
   605	public, no confidentiality constraint binds, and the generator's
   606	contract is exact integer reproduction of every published margin cell
   607	with a declared assumptions register below that grain. We find no
   608	prior public U.S. synthetic customs-entry dataset with that
   609	contract — the combination this paper ships (instrument-cited
   610	executable rules, a conformance verdict against an independent
   611	implementation, and margin-exact public entries) appears to be
   612	unoccupied, and we state the boundary of that claim as a search
   613	bounded at August 2026 rather than a certainty.
   614	
   615	# Data and code availability
   616	
   617	Everything this paper reports predates it in public. The encodings
   618	live in the rulespec-us repository (the tariff composition and its
   619	authority overlays, with mandatory companion tests); the corpus
   620	manifests, comparison harness, conformance reports, and disposition
   621	records in axiom-oracles, with the quoted scoreboard pinned at
   622	snapshot dc1da3af; the entries pipeline, its 149-test battery, and the
   623	committed evidence packs (build report, source manifest, eighteen
   624	per-month reconciliation records, the gated cross-check report) in the
   625	Microcosm repository, merged as pull requests #620 and #621 with the
   626	full adversarial review inventories in their descriptions. The Yale
   627	reference is pinned at commit c4307e51 of Budget-Lab-Yale/
   628	tariff-rate-tracker; our six upstream reports are public issues on
   629	that repository. The Census source archives are public no-auth
   630	downloads whose URL pattern, sizes, and sha-256 digests appear in the
   631	committed source manifest; the CBP page bytes our anchors parse from
   632	are archived beside the facts they ground.
   633	
   634	Replication is therefore not a package assembled for this paper but
   635	the working state of the projects it reports on: re-running the
   636	conformance derivation at the pinned revisions reproduces the
   637	scoreboard; re-running the entries build against the manifested
   638	archives reproduces the artifacts byte-for-byte, a property the review
   639	regime enforced rather than aspired to.
