The paper is not submission-ready. Its pinned numbers mostly reconcile, but its headline claims outrun the demonstrated temporal scope, conformance denominator, legal semantics, and synthetic-data validation.

## Top 10 hostile-expert attacks

1. **[High] Conformance has no auditable denominator — FAILS.** “Every tariff line, partner, and date interval the tracker covers” ([paper.md:217](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:217)) sits beside four unnamed exclusions and 49,200 nonblocking debt intervals. Table 1 reports 10/10 policies, not total, in-scope, covered, matched, or excluded cells. A tripwire prevents drift; it does not justify exclusion. Minimal fix: add a conformance waterfall with all cell counts and percentages, each exclusion’s rationale and footprint, and a sensitivity treating exclusions/debt as failures; narrow the abstract to the evaluated domain.

2. **[High] The authors can award themselves a reference-attributed victory — FAILS.** A disagreement supposedly requires “maintainer acceptance or an independent derivation” ([paper.md:275](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:275)), but “independent” is undefined, Yale has acknowledged neither report, and the paper never partitions the 8,283 cells into classes summing to 8,283. The abstract further calls them simply “two tracker defects” ([paper.md:22](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:22)), violating the derivation-backed-unacknowledged rule. Minimal fix: publish a complete disposition table with class counts, applicability predicates, instruments, adjudicator, and status; report raw mismatches separately; consistently say “author-attributed, derivation-backed, maintainer-unacknowledged discrepancies.”

3. **[High] This is development-time reconciliation, not genuinely external validation — FAILS.** “The validation that matters is external” ([paper.md:204](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:204)) overstates a process iterated against a visible oracle until zero. Yale was separately developed, but both systems share sources, its spine defines the universe, and omissions from that spine cannot be detected. Mutation tests test the comparator, not legal correctness. Minimal fix: call this “cross-implementation reconciliation”; add a frozen held-out snapshot, independently double-coded legal sample, union-of-spines coverage test, or third implementation.

4. **[High] The promised two-endpoint IEEPA model is not evidenced — FAILS.** The abstract promises both endpoints, and §2 says “both endpoints are just versions” ([paper.md:163](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:163)). The pinned code evidence demonstrates only the February 20 legal-zero rule. February 24 comes from CBP CSMS #67834313, not a dated endpoint in EO 14389, and no collection-mode rule/test is shown. Minimal fix: implement and exhibit a separate CSMS-sourced collection-status series, or delete the claim that the operational endpoint survives into the encoded data.

5. **[High] The rate function is formally insufficient — FAILS.** §1 declares four arguments including legal interpretation ([paper.md:78](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:78)); §2 implements only `(line, country, date)` ([paper.md:179](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:179)). That tuple cannot resolve TRQ position, in-transit status, product coverage, or §122’s non-stacking on the §232-covered portion. A date also collapses 12:00/12:01 a.m. boundaries, while `effective_from` alone conflates legal-valid time with publication/knowledge time. Minimal fix: formally define the output and required state—instant, semantic mode, quota/entry attributes, and as-known date—or describe the result narrowly as an ex-post posted nominal rate under Yale’s conventions.

6. **[High] Source excerpts prove provenance, not legal correctness — FAILS.** “Every operative number … traces” to a corpus ([paper.md:185](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:185)), but substring-verified excerpts do not establish completeness, applicability, precedence, exclusions, cross-references, or stacking. “Audit-grade rate lookup for any” covered tuple ([paper.md:495](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:495)) is indefensible given the debt and exclusions. Minimal fix: distinguish citation integrity from semantic validation; add a legal-coding protocol, interaction/precedence table, completeness checklist, and independent legal sample review; replace “audit-grade” with “source-traceable within the stated domain.”

7. **[High] “Exact margins” changes meaning across the paper — FAILS.** The abstract links synthetic entries to “eighteen months reconciled” ([paper.md:25](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:25)), but 18 months describes ingest reconciliation; the generator pilot covers February–June 2026. Public margins are introduced at line × country × district × month, while generator identity covers only district-aggregated line × country × month customs value ([paper.md:378](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:378)). “Every published margin cell” ([paper.md:606](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:606)) is therefore false as written. Minimal fix: separate ingest validation from generator identity everywhere, state the five-month pilot in the abstract, and name the exact reproduced measure and grain.

8. **[High] Aggregate identity is being sold as transaction-level validity — PARTLY SURVIVES.** The limitations are candid, but 3,806,050 weighted rows representing 44,881,145 entries are not one-record-per-transaction data. Within-cell values are lognormal from one imperfect proxy moment, and the fact base reveals every entry date is the 15th. That timing assumption defeats the paper’s own February 20/24 example while §7 claims revenue accounting. “The dataset that downstream tariff microsimulation actually needs” ([paper.md:418](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:418)) is unsupported, especially where proportional duties need no disaggregation. Minimal fix: call these “weighted synthetic entry-line allocations,” define weights and permitted uses, prohibit unqualified intramonth revenue analysis, release alternative distributions/timings, and show downstream sensitivity.

9. **[Medium] The self-review boundary is honest in §3 but not in the abstract or rhetoric — PARTLY SURVIVES.** The paper correctly says the process “is not external certification” ([paper.md:258](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:258)). But “independent … review run to zero findings,” “the trajectory is the evidence,” and “the marginal cost of rigor collapsed” invite a self-certification reading. A final no-finding pass is a stopping outcome, not an error-rate estimate. Minimal fix: consistently call it “same-project cross-model adversarial QA”; disclose models, prompts, stopping rules, human adjudication, and unresolved risks; remove or quantify the productivity claims.

10. **[Medium] The no-first-panel honesty rule survives, but the contribution still lacks venue-level novelty — PARTLY SURVIVES.** “We are not … the first executable statutory tariff panel” ([paper.md:564](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:564)) correctly reflects B9. However, “first external research engagement,” “that culture has not previously reached trade law,” and an “unoccupied” combination remain weak negative-search novelty claims. Minimal fix: state three explicit methodological contributions, compare capabilities systematically with Yale/Teti/rules-as-code validation, and either provide a reproducible search appendix or soften all remaining first/unoccupied language.

## Additional evidence and consistency findings

11. **[High] The advertised period exceeds the usable domain.** “We encode the 2025–26 … stack” ([paper.md:11](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:11)) conflicts with the composed spine beginning in February 2026 ([paper.md:520](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:520)). The synthetic pilot ends in June, so it cannot exercise the July §122/§301 seam or August Revision 15. Minimal fix: state separate rule-history, conformance, margins, and synthetic-entry ranges in the title, abstract, and methods—or extend coverage.

12. **[High] “Public, pinned, and re-runnable” is not delivered.** The example cites mutable `@main` ([paper.md:141](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:141)); RuleSpec and Microcosm lack immutable links/full SHAs; PR descriptions are editable; and there are no commands, environment, schemas, licenses, expected hashes, or archival DOI. Minimal fix: create a replication release with full commits, container/lockfiles, one-command workflows, checksums, data dictionary, prebuilt artifacts, and hardware/runtime requirements.

13. **[High] The manuscript has no functioning citations.** Related-work keys such as `[fajgelbaum2020return]` render literally, there is no References section, and the primary-source BibTeX entries are unused in the legal sections. Minimal fix: enable cite processing, use proper citation syntax, add pinpoint primary citations throughout §§1–4, and render the bibliography.

14. **[Medium] Several universal claims exceed the pinned evidence.** Examples include “Every substantive change” receiving review ([paper.md:448](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:448)), “every escaped cell names its instrument,” solar covering “every affected cell,” and column-2 disagreement touching “every line.” The fact base verifies named review arcs and two legal derivations, not these all-quantifiers. Minimal fix: scope each statement to the named harness/PRs and supply class counts or executable queries for claimed cell footprints.

15. **[Medium] The validation channels are not independent in the claimed sense.** The API is a second Census delivery path, probably backed by the same data, so it can detect parser/channel errors but not common source errors. Likewise, control totals inside the same archives test parsing, not external truth. “Every published measure … in integer dollars” also obscures the 22/18/18 per-axis coverage and quantity measures. Minimal fix: describe channel independence precisely, report sampling strata and coverage, and distinguish monetary from quantity reconciliation.

16. **[Medium] The floating-point exactness claim is too broad.** “At or below 2^53, where integer arithmetic is exact” ([paper.md:380](/Users/maxghenis/TheAxiomFoundation/tariff-paper/paper.md:380)) does not establish safe intermediates or weighted-product exactness. Minimal fix: document the actual integer/BigInt algorithm and intermediate bounds; otherwise use the safe-integer convention and say “exactly representable,” not that generic arithmetic is exact.

17. **[Low] Several factual and labeling repairs remain.** Revision 15 on August 3 was three elapsed days—not four—after July 31; “seven authorities” needs to be “six overlays plus the base schedule” or explicitly enumerated; the six Yale filings are five issues and one PR, not six issues; and “largest action,” “most datasets,” “always,” and “strongest available reference” lack support. Minimal fix: correct, enumerate, or delete these phrases.

## Missing content for publishability

18. **[High] Missing formal methods and an end-to-end worked example.** The paper needs definitions of cell, interval, equality, coverage, debt, exclusion, disposition, semantic mode, time zone, stacking, and version selection; generator equations/algorithm; and one exact HTS-10 example carried from instrument through composition, Yale comparison, synthetic allocation, and computed duty.

19. **[High] Missing a substantive result.** The paper currently describes infrastructure. It needs either a revenue/counterfactual application demonstrating that entry grain and proof-carrying rules materially change an answer, with sensitivity to synthetic assumptions, or explicit repositioning as a software/data-descriptor paper.

20. **[Medium] Missing publication apparatus.** Add an authority timeline, pipeline diagram, conformance waterfall/coverage heat map, and synthetic-distribution sensitivity figure; integrate and cite Tables 1–2; add an explicit contribution/comparison table; replace drafting labels such as “exemplar” and “wire into sections”; fill authorship, funding/conflicts, AI-use disclosure, licenses, and persistent artifact citations.

All numbered section cross-references resolve. Apart from the Revision 14/15 day count, repeated pinned values and hashes agree: 10/10, 8,283, 48,000 + 1,200 = 49,200, 2,396, 138 = 47 + 44 + 47, 108,977, the pilot totals, calibration values, and snapshot identifiers.

